libgcov: give __INTPTR_TYPE__ a fallback for arm-none-symbianelf.

Written for symdev's gcce;12.1.0 recipe from GCC 12.1.0's build error, not copied from
any other change: libgcc/libgcov-driver.c casts a gcov_type to a pointer through
(__INTPTR_TYPE__) (write_topn_counters, lines 457 and 476), but config.gcc gives
arm*-*-symbianelf* no *-stdint.h, so the compiler predefines no __INTPTR_TYPE__ and the
file fails with "'__INTPTR_TYPE__' undeclared".  A pointer is an int on this target,
which is what GCC's config/newlib-stdint.h makes intptr_t (ptrdiff_t's type) on newlib
ARM targets.  The four added lines produce no code; only the debug line numbers of the
code after them move.

This patch modifies a file of GCC and is under GCC's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1

Applied by build.sh with: patch -d gcc-12.1.0 -p1

--- a/libgcc/libgcov-driver.c
+++ b/libgcc/libgcov-driver.c
@@ -412,6 +412,10 @@
 
 #define MAX(X,Y) ((X) > (Y) ? (X) : (Y))
 
+#ifndef __INTPTR_TYPE__
+#define __INTPTR_TYPE__ int
+#endif
+
 /* Store all TOP N counters where each has a dynamic length.  */
 
 static void
